{
 "turns_text": [
  "[SEG0001] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Aoife Murphy, yes. I did her blood pressure on the way in, 128 over 76. Her sister's still in the waiting room, she wanted to come in and all.",
  "[SEG0002] person_2 (DOCTOR): Grand, thanks. Umm, the screen's after freezing again. Have a seat there. What can I do for you?",
  "[SEG0003] person_3 (PATIENT): I'm wrecked, we've been sitting out there forever. It's this pain, up here on the right, after I eat anything greasy.",
  "[SEG0004] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry, say that again? Something beeped.",
  "[SEG0005] person_3 (PATIENT): Pain. Right side of the stomach. Comes on if I have a fry, or cheese, anything fatty. It lasts for hours.",
  "[SEG0006] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right. And how long has that been going on?",
  "[SEG0007] person_3 (PATIENT): A few weeks. Not months. I'm not making it up.",
  "[SEG0008] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): Sorry doctor, can I just, her sister asked me to tell you it's been every day for two months and she can't keep food down at all.",
  "[SEG0009] person_3 (PATIENT): Ah here, that's not right. It is not every day. And I am not throwing up all the time. I got sick the once. A few weeks, like I said.",
  "[SEG0010] person_2 (DOCTOR): Hang on, I lost the thread. Sister says two months and you can't keep food down, you're saying a few weeks and you vomited once. I'll note it as somewhere between a few weeks and two months. You're not agreed.",
  "[SEG0011] person_3 (PATIENT): I'm telling you it's a few weeks. Vomited once, after a takeaway, the whole lot came up. She's fussing, that's all.",
  "[SEG0012] person_2 (DOCTOR): Mm. And where exactly, under the ribs on the right?",
  "[SEG0013] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah. Up under the right ribs. Goes on for hours, then it eases off. The rennys take the edge off a bit.",
  "[SEG0014] person_2 (DOCTOR): Rennys. You mean Rennie, the antacid tablets?",
  "[SEG0015] person_3 (PATIENT): Yeah those. Two of them when it starts. From the chemist. White ones.",
  "[SEG0016] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any fever with these episodes? Temperature up at all?",
  "[SEG0017] person_3 (PATIENT): No. I'm just tired from not sleeping when it hits, that's all. No fever.",
  "[SEG0018] person_2 (DOCTOR): Bowels alright? Any change?",
  "[SEG0019] person_3 (PATIENT): No. They're grand.",
  "[SEG0020] person_2 (DOCTOR): Yellow in the whites of the eyes, or the wee gone dark?",
  "[SEG0021] person_3 (PATIENT): No. Nothing like that.",
  "[SEG0022] person_2 (DOCTOR): Any other medicines, or just the Rennie?",
  "[SEG0023] person_3 (PATIENT): Just them. Nothing else. And I've to be at work for four, so if we could move it along.",
  "[SEG0024] person_2 (DOCTOR): Err, drug reactions. Any medicine you've reacted to?",
  "[SEG0025] person_3 (PATIENT): Penicillin. I came out in a rash all over me and my lips swelled up. They said never take it again.",
  "[SEG0026] person_2 (DOCTOR): Sorry, the screen jumped. Penicillin did what?",
  "[SEG0027] person_3 (PATIENT): A rash all over, and the lips swelled. Years ago. I still don't touch the stuff.",
  "[SEG0028] person_2 (DOCTOR): Right, I'll put that down. Someone said your mam and a gallbladder?",
  "[SEG0029] person_3 (PATIENT): My mam had her gallbladder out. Years back. That's why my sister's losing the head out there.",
  "[SEG0030] person_2 (DOCTOR): Say that again, she had?",
  "[SEG0031] person_3 (PATIENT): Gallbladder surgery. Mam. Not me.",
  "[SEG0032] person_2 (DOCTOR): Do you smoke? Drink?",
  "[SEG0033] person_3 (PATIENT): I don't smoke. A glass of wine at the weekend if even that. I'm too wrecked for the pub, the parking in town is a joke anyway.",
  "[SEG0034] person_2 (DOCTOR): Let me have a feel of the tummy. Tender there, right upper side. No guarding. Soft otherwise.",
  "[SEG0035] person_3 (PATIENT): Ow. Yeah that's the spot. Are you finished poking at me?",
  "[SEG0036] person_2 (DOCTOR): I think this is likely biliary colic, the gallbladder grumbling after the fatty food. I wouldn't call it certain until we have a look.",
  "[SEG0037] person_2 (DOCTOR): I'll book blood tests today and an ultrasound of the gallbladder. If it does not settle we might do a HIDA scan down the line. Let's see you in a fortnight with the results. Lay off the fry-ups, stick with the two Rennie when it starts, paracetamol is fine if you need a painkiller, and no penicillin.",
  "[SEG0038] person_3 (PATIENT): A fortnight. Fine. I'm not touching another takeaway. And can people stop talking for me.",
  "[SEG0039] person_1 (CLINICAL_STAFF): I'll book the ultrasound at the desk, and the bloods are with the nurse this afternoon. Fortnight, I'll put you in."
 ],
